WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:04.822
Lab 1 runs in the provider
notices folder of the examples,

3
00:00:04.822 --> 00:00:09.213
in PowerShell 7, for a fictional
project, contoso example prod.

4
00:00:09.213 --> 00:00:11.601
Nothing signs in or sends a request.

5
00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:14.162
Step one lists what Google Cloud needs.

6
00:00:14.162 --> 00:00:15.150
Two calls.

7
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:19.731
The project call needs the Personalized
Service Health Viewer role on the project,

8
00:00:19.731 --> 00:00:22.387
for the events list
permission, and it's verified.

9
00:00:22.387 --> 00:00:26.145
The organization call needs the
same role on the organization,

10
00:00:26.145 --> 00:00:27.374
and it isn't verified.

11
00:00:27.374 --> 00:00:31.375
Step two collects Google Cloud
from the day-one fixtures:

12
00:00:31.375 --> 00:00:35.375
two notices, one open, none
needing action, both incidents.

13
00:00:35.375 --> 00:00:37.525
Step three reads the records.

14
00:00:37.525 --> 00:00:41.239
Cloud SQL connection errors
in u s east four is open,

15
00:00:41.239 --> 00:00:43.550
with its product and its location.

16
00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:47.300
Cloud Storage latency in
u s central one is closed.

17
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:52.278
None needs action by Google's word,
because Google has no field that says so;

18
00:00:52.278 --> 00:00:57.240
an open incident that names resources
is routed by the agency's own rules.
